// The reset of a simulation to the world it started as, in one goal, for a
// caller that starts its work over on a blank slate. After a reset that
// completes:
// - the scene is the one the simulation opened on, at scale 1, and its
//   objects stand where that scene places them, whole, each under a new
//   object id; no object a caller spawned stands;
// - every robot stands where it came to stand: where the world places it,
//   or where it joined. The reset removes no robot and adds none;
// - the lighting and every material, the robots' materials too, have their
//   authored values, and every camera has its device's defaults;
// - no push acts on any object, and the clock runs. A step in progress
//   ends cancelled, with a reason that names the reset.
//
// Simulated time goes on: it is the clock the simulation's messages are
// stamped with, and it never goes back. What a robot's own nodes hold is
// the robot's, and the reset leaves it: the targets its limbs were last
// sent, which they hold until a robot command moves them, and what its
// gripper is known to hold. A load or a spawn that has not handed its
// command to the engine when the reset comes, one that still fetches its
// files, ends cancelled, with a reason that names the reset, and builds
// nothing.
{
  peppy_schema: "contract/v1",
  manifest: {
    name: "simulation_reset",
    tag: "v1",
  },
  interfaces: {
    actions: [
      {
        // Puts the simulation back as it started, as the header says. The
        // goal completes once the world is rebuilt and runs. A simulation
        // that lets no caller edit its world refuses the reset with
        // `rejected`. The reset fails with `attempt_failed` when the
        // simulation cannot rebuild its world. A refused or failed reset
        // leaves the world as it stood.
        name: "reset",
        goal_service: {},
        result_service: {},
      },
    ],
  },
}
